[00:51.92] We looked toward the woman
[00:54.03] And my face burned red, blushing
[01:00.20] And she asked me the questions
[01:02.59] "Are you ever alone?"
[01:04.56] "Are you younger or older?"
[01:11.46] I held her close
[01:13.55] In my thoughts, some way wanting
[01:16.52] In spite of the sorrow
[01:18.37] My tensing in terror
[01:24.32] On the strip of Ventura
[01:26.83] With the tin barrels burning under a halo of moonlight
[01:31.05] When the hour was lonely
[01:33.05] It was the way that she touched me
[01:35.52] Her arm on the window
[01:37.85] And the way she said, "Baby"
